#!/bin/bash
set -eu
: "${SOBAYA_APP:?}" "${SOBAYA_MODEL:?}" "${SOBAYA_ROLE:?}"
task_dir=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$task_dir"' EXIT
cat > "$task_dir/prompt.txt"
cat >> "$task_dir/prompt.txt" <<'CONTEXT'
The human explicitly approved spec-proposal.md, failed-test-proposal.md, and all exact test replacements in collab/active/codex--reading-experience on 2026-10-16. Read spec.md and failed-test.md/current entry. Implement the current entry using small cohesive source components/hooks with no new dependencies. App source, UI/loading/motion only. Do not edit tests, headers, helpers, fixtures, plans, acceptance commands, package/lockfile, API contracts, Git metadata, harness/runtime/release files. No commits/push/publish/comments. The approved replacement baseline retains106 original tests and the runner restores7 originals under their existing names plus2 new regressions (final115). Every exact input is immutable; unused helper warnings are approved support, not permission to change it.
Requirements: remove search/list load-more buttons, viewport-near infinite scroll with one request at a time; preserve first-seen dedup, raw received offsets, API total, existing cards during pending/error, empty/end stops, explicit error retry only with no observer retry loops, unmount/query stale response and stale callback safety. IntersectionObserver fallback scroll/resize near viewport and cleanup. Keep accessible statuses hidden-text when loading, skeletons decorative and no fake content/links. Implement public loading feedback in cohesive folders, no overengineering.
UI direction: actual Chrome audit confirms Tailwind spacing works. Fix search36px form vs44px controls, use>=44px controls contained inside search form (including borders). Bottom nav side-tab/54px center FAB gap>=8px and keep focus outline visible without overlaps. Suggested chip min36px, explicit6px icon-label gap and RESERVED compact spinner space so chip size changes<1px during actual next/link pending. 16px page gutters, 8–12px related spacing, 20–24px sections; list/search cards12px separation and readable typography. Audit map/list/search/detail/report spacing, adjust actual issues only. Spinner for map SDK/locating, pending link, report submit; skeleton for initial/additional article results/detail. Keep screen-reader text compatible with existing status expectations, preserve error/empty copy and retry. Moderate entry/press/pulse/spinner, ALL stop on prefers-reduced-motion, no layout animation or exaggerated stagger. Preserve default native search/clear, image safety/AI labels, map collision grouping/camera/SDK/filter lifecycle, report input/files/idempotency/timeout/Suspensive boundary. No production POST.
Important runtime limitation: worker sandbox denies sockets required for full suite Next integration tests and Turbopack. Parent Sobaya runner always executes the unchanged full suite and hygiene outside worker sandbox. DO NOT run full suite, build or Next-spawning integration tests in this worker. Run focused jsdom tests for the current entry and relevant source lint/format. Parent handles browser QA/default build/full suite. Return done if coherent source implementation and focused checks are ready; accurately state parent checks remain. Never change tests to avoid sandbox limits. Use package binaries directly for checks if pnpm is unavailable. Format only changed implementation files; never format approved tests/header.
CONTEXT
if [ "$SOBAYA_ROLE" = review ]; then
cat >> "$task_dir/prompt.txt" <<'REVIEW'
Fresh independent READ-ONLY review bound to current HEAD. Review full final diff against the approved baseline and origin/dev; check all spec requirements, infinite scrolling observer lifecycle/unmount/stale callbacks/error pause/one-flight/raw offsets/duplicates/end/fallback, server/client boundaries and loading layouts, accessible role/status/skeleton/spinner, reduced-motion, keyboard/focus geometry, nav safe-area and report flow preservation. Tests/fixtures/API/harness are immutable; current branch intentionally uses approved replacement baseline before materialization. Verify all7 original named regressions restored and2 new ones added. Read browser evidence if present but do not treat worker reports as proof. Do not write/change files or run write-producing tests/builds/commit/publish. Report actionable defects with exact file/line evidence; return done only if none remain.
REVIEW
fi
sandbox=workspace-write
[ "$SOBAYA_ROLE" != review ] || sandbox=read-only
codex exec --cd "$SOBAYA_APP" --model "$SOBAYA_MODEL" --sandbox "$sandbox" -c 'approval_policy="never"' --json --output-schema "$SOBAYA_APP/../sobaya/tdd-set/worker-result.schema.json" --output-last-message "$task_dir/result.json" - < "$task_dir/prompt.txt" > "$task_dir/events.jsonl"
cat "$task_dir/events.jsonl"
if jq -e -s 'any(.[]; .type=="turn.failed" or .type=="error")' "$task_dir/events.jsonl" >/dev/null; then exit 1; fi
jq -c --slurpfile events "$task_dir/events.jsonl" '. + {usage: ([$events[] | select(.type=="turn.completed") | .usage][-1] // {})}' "$task_dir/result.json"
